Source: https://github.com/appium/io.appium.settings at bf8c11b,
lib/commands/geolocation.ts (setGeoLocation, lines 26-75).

What is adapted from it here (issue #851), in Go: how the phone's location is
set on an emulator, in the phone's tools (internal/shared/devicetool,
location.go; internal/node/device/tools.go): each value rounded up to 5
decimals, then `adb emu geo fix <longitude> <latitude> [<altitude>]` sent
twice, the second time with "," in place of "." as a workaround for the
emulator's bug https://code.google.com/p/android/issues/detail?id=206180.
Satellites, speed, bearing and accuracy, and the helper app a real device
needs, are not taken.
